llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: no shrink-wrapping on X86 (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a function whose frame is needed
on one path only. ShrinkWrap (lib/CodeGen/ShrinkWrap.cpp) is in LLVM 3.7
but off by default (lib/CodeGen/Passes.cpp, EnableShrinkWrap(false)); it
was enabled for X86 by r255175 (5d2f7cfd44db, 2015-12-09, "[X86] Enable
shrink-wrapping by default..."), first released in 3.8.0: 3.7.1 sets up
`push rbp; mov rbp, rsp` at entry, 3.8.1 to 5.0.2 below an early test.
The game region was built without it: all 12,521 of its functions that
push rbp do so as their first instruction, no callee-saved push follows
a branch or an exit, and the 78 functions whose early exit needs no frame
(a test before any stack use, branching to `pop rbp; ret`) all keep the
frame at entry; the library region (3.3) likewise (2,101 and 15). With
this patch 0xd8ff10, 0xd8ff30, 0x582360, 0x582380 and 0xc871e0 compile
to the base's bytes and no matched game row changes. The hidden option
-enable-shrink-wrap=false gives the same objects.

--- a/lib/Target/X86/X86FrameLowering.cpp
+++ b/lib/Target/X86/X86FrameLowering.cpp
@@ -2720,16 +2720,9 @@
 }
 
 bool X86FrameLowering::enableShrinkWrapping(const MachineFunction &MF) const {
-  // If we may need to emit frameless compact unwind information, give
-  // up as this is currently broken: PR25614.
-  return (MF.getFunction()->hasFnAttribute(Attribute::NoUnwind) || hasFP(MF)) &&
-         // The lowering of segmented stack and HiPE only support entry blocks
-         // as prologue blocks: PR26107.
-         // This limitation may be lifted if we fix:
-         // - adjustForSegmentedStacks
-         // - adjustForHiPEPrologue
-         MF.getFunction()->getCallingConv() != CallingConv::HiPE &&
-         !MF.shouldSplitStack();
+  // PS4: shrink-wrapping is not enabled for X86, as before LLVM 3.8: the
+  // prologue stays in the entry block and the epilogue in the return blocks.
+  return false;
 }
 
 MachineBasicBlock::iterator X86FrameLowering::restoreWin32EHStackPointers(
